{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Back in the days of my [C]childhood
In the [G]evening when everything was [D]still
I [G]used to sit and listen to the [C]fox hounds
With my [G]dad in the [D]old Kentucky [G]hills
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]I'm on my way back to [C]the old home
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The road winds on up the hill
[G]But there's no light in the [C]window
That [G]shined long [D]ago where I [G]lived
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
Soon my childhood days were over
I had to leave my old home
For my dad and mom were called to heaven
I was left in this world all alone
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
High in the hills of old Kentucky
Stands the fondest spot in my memory
I’m on my way back to the old home
The light in the window I long to see
{end_of_chorus}
